{ Hello everyone!!
We saw 2 openings from white side in the previous study.
Time to destroy from black side now.
We are now going to learn the sicilian dragon variation. One of the most aggressive openings from black side. I have personally tried this openings in many of my games and won many of them .
So let's begin!! } 1. e4 { Play c5 } 1... c5 2. Nf3 { d6 } { [%csl Gd6] } 2... d6 3. d4 { Capture the pawn } 3... cxd4 4. Nxd4 { How can you attack the pawn and develop a piece at the same time? } { [%csl Ge4] } 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { White protects e4 with knight c3 .
Play g6 } 5... g6 { Here we come to the position setup of sicilian dragon, with those pawn resembling shape of a dragon. } { [%csl Gh7,Gg6,Gf7,Ge7,Gd6] } *


