[UTCDate "2021.08.08"]
[UTCTime "15:37:33"]
[Orientation "black"]
[ChapterMode "gamebook"]

{ Now you must be wondering how do we get to that complex position. Don't worry it's easy ! } 1. e4 { I hope you remember the moves } 1... c5 2. Nf3 { Now? } { [%csl Gd6] } 2... d6 3. d4 { Now? } 3... cxd4 4. Nxd4 { Attack that pawn and also develop a piece at the same time } { [%csl Ge4] } 4... Nf6 5. Nc3 { The main move? } 5... g6 6. Be3 { Where was this bishop placed in that position? } { [%csl Gf8] } 6... Bg7 7. f3 { Stopping us from playing knight to g4.
Play knight to c6 } { [%csl Gg4,Gc6][%cal Gb8c6] } 7... Nc6 8. Qd2 { White prepares to castle on queen side.
We castle too! } { [%csl Gc1,Gg8][%cal Ge1c1,Ge8g8] } 8... O-O 9. Bc4 { White developed all his pieces. Play bishop d7 } { [%csl Gd7][%cal Gc8d7] } 9... Bd7 10. O-O-O { Rook to c1 with a semi open file is always strong! } { [%csl Gc8][%cal Ga8c8] } 10... Rc8 { Lookout the white pieces are attacking on the king side.Well but it's a strong defensive position for black.Keep the pieces in coordination to have fair advantage. } { [%cal Gc4g8,Ge3h6,Gd2h6] } *


